"answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative focused on data analytics, cloud storage optimization, and secure file sharing. It was initially introduced with a kickoff scheduled for June 15th (or July 15th in one account) and led by Sarah Tan or Marcus Cole. The project has received significant budget approvals, starting with $500,000 for phase one, later increased to $2 million for all phases, and an additional $15,000 for training. The team expanded with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. Key milestones include the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule, with upcoming phases involving UI enhancements and security protocol updates (effective January next year). Feedback is being sought from stakeholders by the end of November, and the project is described as almost complete."
